# doubt — the player may say NO to what a thinking proposes, and the thinking tries again
#
# High doubt (--doubt high) gives two retries and the doubt. While a retry
# remains, the reasoning ends on a question and the preview box asks YES or NO before the action modus
# mentis is asked. Here the first answer is NO: the mind voices its doubt holding, drops the goal
# with every means and reasons again upon another (at seed 42: climbing back down, then examining the
# tree) — and the second answer is YES (advance answers YES when no `doubt` is queued), which the mind
# voices too. At this seed the acting modus mentis then refuses the examining, so a third try follows,
# its doubt asked while the refusal is still queued in front of it — the stall the CLI's idle test
# once had (CliPreviewAwaitsAnswer). One thinking.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Crown" --period dawn --observe-only "Test Giant Tree" --grant-mm woodcraft --doubt high

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy succeed
advance 12 180

doubt no
click observe "Test Giant Tree"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
click think "Test Giant Tree"
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
# Expected text is matched line by line on the wrapped screen, hence the short fragments.
expect-state texts "But is it truly wise to"
expect-state texts "and it holds"
expect-state texts "another way"
expect-state texts "does not hold"
expect-state texts "I am resolved to"
quit
